# Data conversion between gigabyte and mebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gigabyte and mebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GB to 953.6743MiB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5GB yields 1430.5114MiB; backward, converting 1MiB to 0.0010GB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MiB yields 0.0015GB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GB
print(forward_whole->to(MiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GB
print(forward_fractional->to(MiB))
backward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(backward_whole->to(GB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(backward_fractional->to(GB))

<<< stdout
953.6743MiB
1430.5114MiB
0.0010GB
0.0015GB

<<< stderr
